## 2026-11-18 — ec4375e — add CHANGES.log and Perl test harness

This file (`CHANGES.log`) starts here: one block per commit that changes tracked
content, newest first, with what changed, why, and how it was checked.

Added the Perl harness around the download path under
`scripts/perl_test_harness/`:

    scripts/perl_test_harness/
      README.md
      ghost_soldier_test.pl     one-shot: preflight, download, verify, report
      t/run_all.pl              ordered, resumable suite runner
      t/00_env.t                python / yt-dlp / ffmpeg present and running
      t/10_network.t            Instagram reachable
      t/20_cookie_file.t        cookie file present, 0600, Netscape, has sessionid
      t/30_session.t            cookie session resolves a logged-in profile
      t/40_download.t           real download + SHA256 + output checks (slow)

Why: a single happy-path download proves little; the harness states the
preconditions and checks the artefacts, so a failure says which stage broke.
Suite status at last run (2026-11-18): 00–30 pass, 40 fails with "No video
formats found" for the test post.

Checked:
- `perl -c` on every script and test — syntax OK
- `git ls-files scripts/perl_test_harness | grep -iE 'cookie|credential'`
  — none; the harness reads a cookie path, it carries no cookie

Not included: cookies, and the downloaded media/report the run produces.

